# Parameters of the held-out sample of docs/mutation-push.md (section 9): a fresh sample
# of mutants of the design-of-record core, drawn uniformly per region from Yosys mutate's
# raw database, without the (mode, cell, port) of any mutant of the push's sample or of
# its section 8, and run under the 109-test suite of HEAD_COMMIT. Source campaign.env
# first (its CAMP holds the campaign's design/: base.il, sel/, mutations.tsv), then this
# file, then run the commands of docs/mutation-push.md section 9.6.
#
# the commit whose test tree runs (21 default modules, 109 tests); its
# src/protocol_emulator_core.v is the campaign's core (sha256 26a873db...)
HEAD_COMMIT=56f4b20
# base seed: region k of HELDOUT_QUOTAS (k = 1, 2, ...) uses seed HELDOUT_SEED + k for
# `mutate -list` (its cnot control bits) and for Python's random.Random(...).sample
HELDOUT_SEED=20260930
# 80 % of each region quota of campaign.env, in its order (1,936 mutants)
HELDOUT_QUOTAS=engine_ctrl=440,host=320,mover=200,events=240,pins=200,engine_xfer=160,imem=48,shared=72,fifo=104,engine_data=144,timestamp=8
# excluded besides the campaign's mutations.tsv: the eight mutants of section 8
HELDOUT_EXCLUDE_EXTRA=campaigns/mutation/results/heldout-56f4b20/exclude_section8.tsv
# the work directory as run, and a fresh one for a re-run
HELDOUT_DIR=${PE_WORK:?set PE_WORK to the cluster work directory}/mut-heldout
HELDOUT=${PE_WORK:?set PE_WORK to the cluster work directory}/mutation-heldout
# formal_mutant.py options: the push's (job 23977941) and the longer cap of its section 4.5
FORMAL_ARGS="--props strict --pdr-seconds 60 --abc-timeout 150"
FORMAL_LONG_ARGS="--props strict --pdr-seconds 600 --abc-timeout 900"
# controls (held-out ids, random.Random(20260930)): for the miter, six killed by test_smoke
# and six proven by equiv_mutant.py; for equiv_inv.py, three more killed by test_smoke
HELDOUT_FORMAL_CONTROLS="568 673 835 1224 1686 1697 145 379 1017 1195 1554 1796"
HELDOUT_EINV_CONTROLS="1104 1260 1636"
# Simulator: run_mutant.py puts $PE_WORK/cocotb/bin first on PATH; for the simulation
# stages of this run that directory held the Icarus Verilog 13.0 wrappers (iverilog, vvp),
# and $PE_WORK/cocotb/venv20 the cocotb 2.0.1 environment, as in CI.
